Subject: Modeling Algorithms - BRepGProp_Face splits a surface of revolution's U into three spans, as a torus's
Upstream: ISSUE-TO-COME (the issue the maintainer posts on BRepGProp_Gauss's U refinement; a PR needs OCCT's CLA)
Applies to: OCCT V7_9_3.
Why: BRepGProp_Gauss::Compute with an Eps (BRepGProp::VolumeProperties(shape, props, eps),
     Silico's precise measure) never refines U: EpsU is left 0, so the U loop ends after its
     first pass, and U is integrated once over the spans BRepGProp_Face::UKnots gives. Those
     are thirds for a cylinder, cone, sphere, or torus, and one span for anything else, a
     GeomAbs_SurfaceOfRevolution included, whose U is the same angle over [0, 2*pi]. So a
     full turn of an arc whose circle crosses the axis (a barrel, a dome) measured 2.2e-7
     low, and of a multi-span B-spline 3.9e-6 low; with three spans, both to round-off. The
     default integration (Compute without an Eps, FreeCAD's) reads neither UKnots nor
     SUIntSubs, and is unchanged to the bit.
Drop when: Silico upgrades to an OCCT release that splits or refines a surface of revolution's
     U (check BRepGProp_Face::UKnots and BRepGProp_Gauss::Compute).

--- a/src/BRepGProp/BRepGProp_Face.cxx
+++ b/src/BRepGProp/BRepGProp_Face.cxx
@@ -283,6 +283,10 @@
     case GeomAbs_Torus:
       N = 4;
       break;
+    case GeomAbs_SurfaceOfRevolution:
+      // U is an angle over [0, 2*pi], as a torus's: three spans.
+      N = 4;
+      break;
     case GeomAbs_BezierSurface:
       N = 2;
       break;
@@ -345,6 +349,7 @@
     case GeomAbs_Cone:
     case GeomAbs_Sphere:
     case GeomAbs_Torus:
+    case GeomAbs_SurfaceOfRevolution:
       Knots(1) = 0.0;
       Knots(2) = M_PI * 2.0 / 3.0;
       Knots(3) = M_PI * 4.0 / 3.0;
